; node_run.exe ARGS runs `node ARGS`, if node is in PATH and its version is
; 22.3.0 or later. If not, it writes "SKIP: no node" and gives exit status 0,
; but 1 if KILIM_REQUIRE_NODE is 1 (CI). Each rule of the aliases runtest and
; browsers that runs node uses it, thus `dune build @runtest` passes with no
; node (an opam install with the tests). Each of these rules has the dependency
; (env_var KILIM_REQUIRE_NODE).
;
; The minimum version: node 20 has no WebAssembly GC, thus the wasm_of_ocaml
; tests do not start. Node 22.0.0 runs them, but test/browser and test/weak
; use process.getBuiltinModule, which came in node 22.3.0. All the tests pass
; with node 22.3.0.
;
; --or-copy FILE: if node does not run, write FILE to stdout. The CSP rule of
; src/loader gives the hash to stdout, then compares it with loader.csp.

(library
 (name node_version)
 (modules node_version))

(executable
 (name node_run)
 (modules node_run)
 (libraries node_version unix))

; The parser of `node --version`, with pre-release versions.

(test
 (name test_node_version)
 (modules test_node_version)
 (libraries node_version))
